{
	title: 'Antigravity (agy) as a Hal model through ACP',
	spec: "Model ids agy/<model> (gemini-4-neon, gemini-3.8-flash, ...) run Google's unmodified agy CLI as an Agent Client Protocol server (agy acp --disable-telemetry, plus --dangerously-skip-permissions only when config setting agyPermissions is 'skip'), one process per Hal session, started on its first agy request, so a Google AI subscription works in Hal under Google's own login; Hal never handles Google credentials. Hal exposes its non-file/shell tools (HELP, SEND, SPAWN, INSPECT, READ_ENTRY, WAIT, STOP, COMMAND, COMPACT, NOTIFY, EVAL, BRAVE, MCP, plugins, filtered by the session's allowed tools, with template-rendered help descriptions, readOnlyHint annotations, and stripped agy toolSummary unless declared) over a per-session loopback TCP MCP bridge via --ide-mcp-port when nc is available (per-socket UTF-8 decoders, drain-backed write queuing for large responses, EOF tail flushing, and notifications/tools/list_changed on plugin hot-reload). agy keeps its own conversation and runs its own tools: Hal sends only unseen user input as ACP text and image content blocks (skipping hosted-tool replay notes structurally via TextBlock.hosted rather than regex, so tool outputs containing </hal-note> never leak), reuses the live ACP session when the last prompt is edited (matching persisted basePrefix/baseHash in agy.ason and prepending an edited-prompt hal-note), treats all hosted_tool blocks as effectful in prompts.harmless so edits and /edit undo never rewind past agy tools, skips Hal pruning for externalContext providers so agy's prefix hash never mutates, uses live turn.context for contextNotice instead of cumulative turn usage, and starts a fresh agy session seeded with a bounded text+image transcript (capping hosted-tool notes at maxHostedSeedChars and total seed text at maxSeedChars, well under agy's ~192 KB USER_REQUEST cap, prioritizing the current prompt and newest turns, and wrapping tool-only turns cleanly) whenever history genuinely diverges (compact, rebase, earlier edit, fork, cwd change, another model's turn). The agy session id, account (updated in agy.ason when learnEmail learns a missing email), seen history prefix and edit base persist in agy.ason (not copied by fork); after a restart or idle stop, Hal resumes via session/resume and falls back to transcript seeding on failure. Mid-turn steering (Enter, Ctrl-Enter, SEND) injects a new session/prompt into the running ACP session without session/cancel; Stop sends session/cancel and awaits settlement before the next prompt. Hal disables automatic retry of failed agy rounds (noAutoRetry) so failures surface directly with complete RPC errors, full drained stderr, and an agy acp --login hint on auth errors; on host restart, turn-recovery continues unfinished agy turns via session/resume like other providers. agy tool calls become hosted_tool blocks with ToolPresentation cards (clean shell commands, numbered diffs via textDiff, file reads/searches, and Hal MCP tools mapped back to native cards with captured output). Host startup refreshes agy's model catalog, display names and per-model effort levels (low, medium, high, xhigh, max via variants and thought_level). Context and usage come strictly from agy's usage_update and prompt result usage, displaying unknown when none has been reported. Idle agy processes stop after 15 minutes (and on tab close, host exit, or reset); reopening a tab never spawns agy. Hal's rendered system prompt, minus <cwd>/AGENTS.md which agy loads itself, rides on session/new and session/resume as _meta.antigravity.systemPrompt.append. session/request_permission follows agyPermissions: 'hal' (default) answers like Hal's own tools under the security setting (commands matching approval.findings ask the user, or are rejected when unattended; reads of approval.sensitive paths are rejected; the rest is allowed; security yolo allows all); 'ask' opens Hal's approval question UI for every request. The MCP bridge runs Hal tools only during the session's agy turn and, on Linux, refuses connections from other OS users. A session whose tool list excludes bash, or an untrusted project with <cwd>/AGENTS.md or GEMINI.md, gets an error instead of an agy turn, since agy's own tools and instruction loading ignore both. /model and /cd during an agy turn cancel it like Stop; a steer does not. Updates for other ACP sessions are ignored. Covered by an offline e2e test replaying a recorded ACP session (prompt, tool cards, cancel, and resume after restart). Rationale: Google allows subscription use only through its own agent binary spoken to over ACP; extracting or proxying its tokens risks account suspension. Several Google accounts are first-class in secrets/auth.ason (agy-accounts.ts, login-agy.ts): agy holds non-secret references ({ email, keychain: true } for agy's Keychain login, or { email, geminiDir } run with --gemini-dir and SSH_CONNECTION so agy stores its token file there while HOME stays the user's); Hal stores no Google secrets and learns missing emails from agy's ACP log without touching the Keychain. /login agy (in picker and completion, and offered by intro.ts when agy is available) runs SSH_CONNECTION=... agy acp --gemini-dir <new dir> --login, shows the OAuth URL, reads the pasted code from a secret field, sends it to stdin, parses 'Logged in as <email>.' and records the entry; /logout removes entries by slot (y1, y2, ...). /status lists agy accounts with slots, * on the session's account, limited-until deadlines and verification holds with links; /account uses slot ids; stats.plan shows the session's agy slot on the status row. A session stays on its account (agy.ason survives restarts). agy's reply text '⚠ Individual quota reached. ... Resets in 1h35m49s.' becomes a clean 429 (reset carried via retryAt, no raw JSON body) that sets the account aside in limits.ason and retries on the next account in a fresh transcript-seeded session; when every non-verification account is spent, the turn waits for the earliest reset. When agy collapses a backend error (such as Google 403 PERMISSION_DENIED VALIDATION_REQUIRED with validation_url) into a bare '⚠ ...' message chunk and end_turn, agy-log.ts reads that process's ACP log slice since turn start, surfaces the full failure (status, reason, message, verify link) as a turn error instead of a completed reply, records a persistent verification hold in limits.ason (no reset time; cleared on a later successful request on that account or /login agy), and rotates to the next non-verification account when one exists (ending in error when none does).",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Checked by hand 2026-11-23 against agy 1.5.15 with a scratch home: a first prompt edited a file through agy; after a host restart the transcript seed let agy answer about the earlier turn; a following prompt on the live host reused the agy process and session (agy's ACP log: one session/new, two session/prompt). agy's session/new lists model ids with effort suffixes (gemini-4-neon-high) and also Claude Opus/Sonnet 5.5. Not yet checked: stop mid-turn, switching to another model and back. No tests yet: first playable, experimental.",
		"Open (review by 14-huh, openai/gpt-6.2-astra): Hal's automatic retries after a failed agy turn send 'continue' to an agy that may already have done the work; agy supports session/load and resume, unused; Hal's approval UI is unused (permissions skipped); SPAWN with an agy model would not honor tools restrictions.",
		"Resume checked by hand 2026-11-23: after a host restart agy's log showed session/resume and no session/new, and the model recalled a word from before the restart.",
		'Step 1 (2026-11-23): Hal tools (send, spawn, inspect, read_entry, wait, stop, command, compact, notify, eval, brave, mcp, plugins) exposed to agy acp over --ide-mcp-port loopback TCP MCP bridge (src/host/agy-mcp.ts); verified against agy 1.5.15 calling inspect host.',
		'Step 2 (2026-11-23): Mid-turn steering (both Enter/steer and Ctrl-Enter/SEND soft-steer) injects a second session/prompt directly into agy acp without session/cancel; agy finishes any in-flight tool and steers the running turn. Verified against agy 1.5.15.',
		'Step 3 (2026-11-23): Stop sends session/cancel, clears in-flight tool tracking, and awaits cancel settlement (with 5 s bound) before the next session/prompt. Verified against agy 1.5.15: Stop pauses cleanly and an immediate next prompt succeeds in the same ACP session.',
		'Step 4 (2026-11-23): Added Provider.noAutoRetry (true for agy) so Hal never auto-retries failed agy turns or auto-continues unfinished agy turns on host restart; failures show directly to the user.',
		'Step 5 (2026-11-23): Pasted images and tool-result images are sent as ACP image content blocks ({ type: "image", data, mimeType }) instead of "[image omitted]"; pastes/files continue via Hal blob expansion. Verified against agy 1.5.15 identifying a red PNG attachment.',
		'Step 6 (2026-11-23): agy tool calls render as readable Hal tool cards in terminal and web via ToolPresentation on HostedToolBlock (src/host/agy-cards.ts): bash commands with stripped agy timestamps, numbered diffs via textDiff, read/search cards, and Hal MCP tools mapped back to native Hal cards with captured output.',
		'Step 7 (2026-11-23): Full error and stderr pass-through: flush trailing stderr lines and drain stderr before reporting process exit, report spawn failures with command/cwd without leaking MCP sockets, format JSON-RPC error code/message/data with stderr, and append an `agy acp --login` hint on expired/missing auth errors.',
		'Step 8 (2026-11-23): Model catalog and effort mapping moved to src/host/agy-models.ts; host startup refreshes agy models (via `agy models`) with display names and per-model effort levels (low/medium/high/xhigh/max -> Low/Medium/High/Extra/Max), also synced from session/new and thought_level configOptions.',
		'Step 9 (2026-11-23): Context and usage come strictly from what agy reports: usage_update gives live context occupancy (`used`) and per-model context window (`size`), result.usage gives cumulative turn token counts (input, cacheRead, cacheWrite, output). When agy has reported nothing yet, stats.contextUnknown shows "context unknown" (terminal/web details), "unknown" (web overview/INSPECT) instead of a hardcoded 0/1049k.',
		'Step 10 (2026-11-23): Process lifecycle: idle agy processes stop after agy.idleTimeoutMs (default 15 min, unrefed timer) and resume transparently via agy.ason on the next prompt; tab close, host exit, and host.reset stop agy processes without loading agy.ts unless used; reopening a tab never spawns agy.',
		'Step 11 (2026-11-23): Added agyPermissions setting ("skip" default, "ask" for Hal approval UI). In "ask" mode agy acp runs without --dangerously-skip-permissions and session/request_permission opens Hal’s question UI via src/host/agy-approval.ts + /approve (defaulting to Deny, highlighting dangerous shell commands). Extracted prompt/prefix helpers to src/host/agy-prompt.ts. Verified against agy 1.5.15.',
		'Step 12 (2026-11-23): Verified against agy 1.5.15: agy reads <cwd>/AGENTS.md automatically, but not parent-directory AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md. agyPrompt.extraInstructions sends only the trusted project/global instructions agy misses (~/.agents/AGENTS.md, parent AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md) with the first prompt of a fresh ACP session without duplicating <cwd>/AGENTS.md.',
		'Step 13 (2026-11-23): Added offline e2e test in src/e2e.test.ts replaying recorded agy 1.5.15 ACP fixture (src/fixtures/agy-acp.jsonl) covering prompt, recorded run_command/edit_file tool cards, mid-turn cancel + follow-up, and session/resume after Ctrl-R host restart.',
		"Fixes after review by 54-inf (openai/gpt-6-astra), 2026-11-23. Invariants restored: (1) agy sessions get Hal's system prompt (USER.md, rules, SPAWN systemPrompt), which agy 1.5.15 accepts as _meta.antigravity.systemPrompt.append, verified by hand; (2) Hal tools run only for the session's own turn and OS user; (3) /model and /cd stop the old agy turn; (4) agy's commands get Hal's best-effort approval by default: without --dangerously-skip-permissions agy 1.5.15 asks for every run_command and for reads outside the workspace, never for edits inside it, so tool-restricted sessions without bash are refused; (5) untrusted project instructions never reach agy; (6) a turn aborted before session/prompt still schedules the idle stop. The e2e agy test now waits for the fourth turn end before asserting, fixing a flaky failure.",
		'Appended instruction to agyPrompt.system telling agy to write file paths as plain inline code instead of markdown file:// links (session 54-lib).',
		'Host-restart recovery (54-nay, 2026-11-24): removed the noAutoRetry block from turn-recovery.ts (and reverted the over-engineered restart-provenance/resumeOnly commit a6960378). Invariant: noAutoRetry stops automatic retries of failed agy RPC rounds in turns.ts, while host restarts resume interrupted agy turns via session/resume like other providers; agyPrompt strips hosted-tool notes without dropping sibling continue notices.',
		"Bug fix (54-oak, 2026-11-23): inTurnSteer previously aborted agy's turnSignal with jobs.steered on advisory subagent reports and mid-turn messages, which killed in-flight MCP WAIT calls synchronously with 'Wait stopped by a new user message' before subagents.report woke WAIT. Invariant restored: agy keeps a turn-scoped AbortController (turnAbort) alive across inTurnSteer so MCP tools and permission prompts abort only on real cancellation (Pause/Stop, /model, /cd, exit, or turn end); work.wait also wakes cleanly on delivered prompt events for self and triggers inTurnSteer when promoting queued messages during WAIT.",
		"Accounts (2026-11-24, agy 1.5.15): agy keeps its login in the macOS login Keychain via /usr/bin/security (zalando go-keyring), so --gemini-dir alone does not isolate it. A separate HOME with its own login.keychain-db did, but agy runs commands in an in-process shell that inherits HOME, so ~ in its commands pointed into the account dir; rejected. agy's shouldBypassKeyring takes SSH_CONNECTION as 'no keyring' and stores the token in <gemini-dir>/antigravity-cli/antigravity-oauth-token (mode 600); checked: a fresh gemini dir with SSH_CONNECTION was logged out while the same without it got the Keychain login. Quota arrives as agent_message_chunk text, not an ACP error; seen once as a single chunk. If agy ever splits it, the text shows and the turn ends normally (loud, not silent). Checked by hand in a scratch home: account default hit its quota, the round retried on lex, whose commands saw the real HOME.",
		"First-class agy accounts & visible errors (15-isp, 2026-11-24): verified against agy 1.5.15 binary and real ACP log that agy formats agent executor errors as '\\n⚠ %s\\n' agent_message_chunk with stopReason end_turn and empty stderr, logging the full Google 403 PERMISSION_DENIED / VALIDATION_REQUIRED JSON and validation_url only to <gemini-dir>/antigravity-cli/log/acp-server-*-<pid>.log. Invariants restored: (1) Hal never hides agy backend errors or ends them as completed replies—agy-log.ts reads the turn's ACP log slice to surface the full status, reason, message and verify URL; (2) accounts requiring verification are held in limits.ason without a reset time (shown in /status with the link, skipped by rotation unless explicitly picked via /account or all accounts need verification, cleared on success or /login agy); (3) secrets/auth.ason holds only non-secret agy references ({ email, keychain } / { email, geminiDir }), with /login agy, /logout, /status, /account (y1/y2), stats.plan, intro wizard, and clean 429 errors without raw JSON body.",
		"Bridge reliability & edited messages (15-nah, 2026-11-24): fixed 5 bugs found on real agy 1.5.15 sessions. Invariants restored: (1) editing the last prompt stays on the live ACP session (persisted basePrefix/baseHash in agy.ason) and resends with an edited-prompt hal-note instead of re-seeding; (2) prompts.harmless treats all hosted_tool blocks as effectful so edits/undo never rewind past agy tools; (3) hosted-tool replay notes carry structural TextBlock.hosted (no non-greedy </hal-note> regex), so tool output containing </hal-note> never leaks into subsequent prompts; (4) agyPrompt.seed caps hosted-tool seed text (maxHostedSeedChars) and total seed text (maxSeedChars = 120k, well below agy's ~192 KB USER_REQUEST cap), keeping the newest prior messages and always preserving the current prompt, and splits on assistant or hosted-tool messages so tool-only turns wrap cleanly; (5) pruning.project skips externalContext providers so agy's prefix hash never mutates on turn checkpoints/pressure, contextNotice uses live turn.context instead of cumulative agy turn usage, and learnEmail persists the learned email back to agy.ason so session/resume matches after restart.",
		"MCP bridge improvements (14-jag, 2026-11-24): exposed HELP over agy-mcp (only bash/read/edit/grep stay excluded so agy's own tools remain under agy-approval); rendered MCP tool descriptions via nativeTool.guide + systemPrompt.template instead of regex-stripping ::: lines; annotated read-only tools with readOnlyHint; stripped agy's injected toolSummary unless declared in the tool schema; replaced shared TextDecoder and unchecked socket.write with per-socket TextDecoder, EOF tail flushing, and a drain-backed write queue so large text/image responses never truncate; broadcast notifications/tools/list_changed on plugin hot-reload; cleared agent.mcpResults on session/new and cancelTurn; added unit/loopback contract tests in src/host/agy-mcp.test.ts."
	],
	needs: []
}
